# DRIP project / issue structure (durable)

Canonical product rules for notes vs projects. Code lives under `src/document/project/`. Do not invent conflicting folder layouts or renumber `f-#` / `i-#`.

## KB contents

| Zone | Allowed metadata types |
|------|------------------------|
| **Notes** (outside any `.p`) | `concept`, `task` only |
| **Projects** (inside `.p`) | `project`, `feature`, `issue`, `task` |
| Removed from product defaults | `decision`, `implementation` |

## Project folder whitelist (`Name.p/`)

Only these children:

1. `_Name.p.d.txt` — project index  
2. `_issues.d.txt` — project issue inbox (create/nest new issues here)  
3. Feature folders `*.f/` **or** feature files `*.f.d.txt`  

No other files or folders. Enforce on create/drag + diagnostics.

## Stable entity ids (never renumber existing)

- Features: `f-1`, `f-2`, … project-scoped; stamped on create into feature h0; monotonic counter in `index_meta`
- Issues: `i-1`, `i-2`, … project-scoped; heading type prefix is **`.i-N`** (e.g. `# .i-34 Fix login`). Never put `i-N` in the editable RHS title. **Next id = max(live issues in project) + 1** — deleting the highest (e.g. `i-10`) reuses that number after the index updates; never renumber existing headings; do not fill middle gaps.
- Storage: live ids from `index.drip` issue headings; `index_meta` key `project_entity_alloc_<prefix>` caches `{ nextIssue, nextFeature }` (feature counter still monotonic). 

## Two parents (do not conflate)

| Kind | Storage | Meaning |
|------|---------|---------|
| Outline | indented section (rule below) → `headings.parent` (same-file heading_id) | Visual nesting in one file |
| Issue link | issue attribute `parent: i-N` → `issue_metadata.parent_issue_key` | Logical parent anywhere in the project |

After an issue is **moved** to a feature mailbox, outline parent may be gone; **`parent: i-N` must remain** so Project View can rebuild hierarchy.

## Hierarchy

```
project
  ├─ features (f-#)
  │    └─ issues (after assign/sort) → nested issues → tasks
  └─ _issues.d.txt
         └─ issues (i-#) → nested issues → tasks
```

## Mailbox (assign = move)

1. Create issues in Project View → `_issues.d.txt`, as the **last** child of a plain (non-persistent) `# recents` heading placed 2 blank lines under `---` (one section only). Sub-issues from Project View are indented under their parent heading (in whichever project file it lives) — no `parent:` line.  
2. Assign to feature → **move** block into:
   - folder feature → `Feature.f/_recent.d.txt`  
   - file feature → last child (one tab in) of the `# _recent` section (2 blank lines under `---`) in `Feature.f.d.txt`  
3. Preserve `parent: i-N` and the heading type prefix `.i-N`  
4. User sorts from `_recent` into feature sections

**Where an issue ends (one rule everywhere):** an issue owns every following line indented deeper than its heading; the first non-blank line (text, identity line or heading) at the same or a shallower indent ends it (the `---` header separator never does). Moves, sub-issue inserts and MCP reads use `sectionEnd`; outline parents (index `headings.parent` → `parent_issue_key`, RHS lock, diagnostics) use `outlineParentsByLine` — both in `issueInboxLayout.js`.  

Project View: features listed; bottom = remaining `_issues.d.txt` inbox; full tree uses `parent: i-#` across files.

## Index tables (v14)

| Table | Role |
|-------|------|
| `projects` | One row per `.p` folder (`project_id`, `folder_prefix`) |
| `headings` | Shared for notes + projects; `project_id` NULL outside `.p`, set inside (do **not** split into two headings tables — embeddings/refs stay unified) |
| `issues` | Canonical issue rows: `(project_id, issue_key)`, `parent_issue_key`, status/priority/… |
| `issue_metadata` | Typed-column mirror on ingest (same hot keys); Project View reads `issues` |

Next issue id = max(live `issues.issue_key`) + 1 for that project.

